ems that dying for a weirwood  tree provides a kind of afterlife  death before a weirwood tree is no death  at all your consciousness is transferred  into the weirwood tree net you become  one with the roots of the trees one with  nature and the forest itself and all the  animals that live in and  children of the forest was the name  given to them by the first men but it is  not their true name they called  themselves those who sing the song of  Earth in the true tongue a language  which no human can speak so what does  their name mean the children called upon  the old gods with prayer grisly  sacrifice and song and many cultures and  religions in our own world songs are  used as a way of communing with higher  planes of existence a way of  transcending the physical we know that  in our story songs can be used for  ritual purposes Mary mazdoor uses songs  to conjure shadows and Drogo's tit and  later sayings to create the spell which  seems to have saved Danny from burning a  song can be a spell it seems if we look  at the actual definitions of the word  song we see that it can be defined as  the musical phrases uttered by some  birds whales and insects typically  forming a recognizable and repeated  sequence and used chiefly for  territorial defense this definition  suggests that the children view  themselves as the defenders of Earth the  key difference between mankind and the  children is that men live on the earth  and the children live with the earth the  children plant no seeds they farm no  animals they take only what they need  from the land men on the other hand  destroy forests for shelter they hunt  animals to extinction such as the  unicorns and the Lions of Westeros the  point is that the children viewed  mankind is huge offenders against nature  their territory a conflict was  inevitable when the children realized  that they were losing the war drastic  measures were required so the children  are the defenders of nature and they  also sing the songs and the spells of  Earth and the old gods stirred and  Giants awoke in the earth and all of  Westeros trembled it is said that Giants  awoke in the earth when the children  sang their songs and conjured the hammer  of the waters on the Isle of faces does  this mean literal Giants seems unlikely  to me the phrase Giants awoke from the  earth is mentioned more than once in a  Song of Ice and Fire  Sherman who blew the Horn of winter and  Wolf Giants from the earth Jon Snow 3 a  clash of kings  the Horn of Joramun is a legendary horn  created by the children it is believed  to have a power to somehow bring down  the wall  it looks like Giants waking from the  earth is a metaphor for earthquakes  what else could bring down a giant ice  wall what else could rip the arm of  Dorne into shreds and break the neck of  Westeros into pieces from what we know  of the children most of their power  stems from the weirwood trees somehow  and the power of the trees seems to be  fuelled by blood the likeness between  the sap of the trees and blood has  brought up multiple times throughout our  story it looks like that in order to  harness the power of the earth a  sacrifice must be made a sacrifice to  the trees and if the children were using  their own young as the world of Ice and  Fire suggests then this could be related  to their small numbers which dwindled  from small to almost none during the  feud with mankind did the children out  of desperation make the ultimate  sacrifice killing off their own young in  an attempt to stop mankind from claiming  the forest it seems to fit the pattern  of situational irony in the story of the  children versus men the children kill  their own young to break the world and  end up causing their numbers to dwindle  even further it's also possible that in  A Song of Ice and Fire  the children use their own young to  create the others which backfires and  leads to the long night the ones who  sing the songs of Earth are their own  undoing in this series it has been  demonstrated again and again that  sorcery is costly in a dance with  dragons Milla saundra mentions the cost  of her power it was an art and like all  arts it demanded mastery discipline  study pain that to release Boake to his  chosen ones through blessed fire in the  language of ash and cinder and twisting  flame that only a god could truly grasp  and Milla saundra had practiced her art  for years beyond count and she had paid  the price blood trickled down her thigh  blackened smoking  the fire was inside her and agony and  ecstasy filling her searing her  transforming her Milla saundra says the  fire is searing her transforming her if  she is truly using a glamour to appear  younger than she is then this seems to  suggest that she is in constant pain  from a fire within all to maintaining a  glamour marry masseur mentions the costs  of magic as well stating to Daenerys  multiple times that only death can pay  for life  beric Dondarrion has left more empty and  Hollow each time he is resurrected and  eventually he chooses willingly to die  brands power was born only when he fell  from the tower and broke his legs  Arya's power was only truly awoken when  she was blinded payment must be made a  trade of source the ones who sang the  songs of earth traded in blood the blood  of their own young and it was key in  their doom
 

